  "description": "<strong>London's most mind-bending summer experience. Now 25% OFF every day 9:00 AM–10:00 AM and 5:15 PM–7:30 PM 😎</strong><br>\r\n<br>\r\n⭐ <em>Exit reality. Enter fun at Paradox Museum London! Step into 50+ hands-on illusions, interactive rooms and reality-defying photo moments in Knightsbridge, directly opposite Harrods. This summer, </em><strong><em>Paradox Pier</em></strong><em> has landed! A limited-time seaside-inspired experience where hidden clues, playful surprises and the new </em><strong><em>Paradox Postcard Trail</em></strong><em> appear across the museum. Go tiny or giant in the Ames Room, get lost in the Mirror Maze, walk through the Tube Room, defy gravity and capture photos your friends won’t believe are real. Perfect for families, friends, tourists and anyone looking for a fun indoor London day out this summer.</em><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Add-Ons</strong><br>\r\n🏖 <em>Paradox Postcard Trail</em>: find the beach in Knightsbridge! Pick up your Impossible Postcard, hunt for hidden seaside clues across selected exhibits, match them to your postcard and claim your Paradox Pier prize at the gift shop. Available for a limited time this summer.<br>\r\n🌀 <em>Zero Gravity Room</em>: Defy balance, movement, and gravity! Complete your mission, capture a video, and take home a verified souvenir pass. 🚀<br>\r\n🔄<em> Flex Ticket</em>: Make your ticket flexible and <strong>reschedule your visit anytime</strong> on the same day. Limited capacity, pre-booking recommended. One add-on per person.&nbsp;<br>\r\n🛍️ <em>Merch Bundle </em>: <strong>Save 25%</strong> on souvenirs online! Includes a Bendy Pencil, Paradox Hourglass, Mind Game Puzzle and Paradox Spinner!<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Highlights</strong><br>\r\n🌏 Visited by 3 million people worldwide<br>\r\n🤯 Explore 50+ immersive paradoxes and challenge reality<br>\r\n👪 Play in impossible rooms: stand upside down, disappear, and snap epic selfies!<br>\r\n🤳 Experience the Zero Gravity Room: feel like you're walking in space! (add-on required)<br>\r\n🧠 Challenge yourself and think outside the box<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Additional Information</strong><br>\r\n⏳ Duration: approx. 90 minutes<br>\r\n📍 Location: Paradox Museum London<br>\r\n👤 Age: All ages welcome! Children must be accompanied by a paying adult. Photo ID required for minors aged 14–17. Children under 4 enter for free. All visitors, including toddlers and infants, require a valid ticket. Admission may be refused if you arrive without tickets for all members of your group and we are fully booked.<br>\r\n🌀 Those under 18 require adult consent for the Zero Gravity experience.<br>\r\n🎁 Gift memories to someone special! Purchase a gift card <a href=\"https://feverup.com/m/182678\">here</a><br>\r\n👉 Plan a birthday party at Paradox Museum <a href=\"https://feverup.com/m/367302/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br>\r\n♿ Accessibility: wheelchair accessible. Please check the FAQs, some exhibits are not fully accessible<br>\r\n❓&nbsp;Consult the FAQs <a href=\"https://paradoxmuseum.com/london/#faqs\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<strong>Description</strong><br>\r\nStep into Paradox Museum London and see the world from a new perspective. Discover mind-bending exhibits like the Infinity Well, the Zero Gravity Room, the Paradox Sofa, and the Paradox Tunnel, where reality is redefined and gravity is defied. Each exhibit challenges your perception and creativity. Get your tickets now for this immersive experience!",
